    "body": "Closes #35.\n\n## What the issue asked for\n\n> We should make sure we have support for greetings of users with hi/hello or greetings stickers, like we did in https://github.com/konard/vk-bot\n> …\n> We should support it in VK, Telegram and other systems we already support. We also should try to do the same in x, whatsapp, zalo, and others.\n>\n> In telegram for example we should try to use the same default greeting stickers, that are possible to use when dialog is empty, and also other greeting stickers (which user should be able to select and see in the UI), we should not import any graphics file in our repository, but we can store direct links to them.\n>\n> If not possible to collect in advance, we should use API to list them.\n\n## What this PR adds\n\nThe case study maps each requirement to the code and archives the research behind it: [`docs/case-studies/issue-35/`](https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/blob/issue-35-9b770690b2d5/docs/case-studies/issue-35/README.md).\n\n- **`js/src/greetings/`**, a new subsystem:\n  - **`catalog.js`** records what each network allows: how a sticker is addressed, whether stickers can be listed live, and who can be greeted. Networks: VK, Telegram, WhatsApp, Messenger, Zalo, X, email.\n    - VK: the 43 greeting sticker ids from vk-bot's `stickers/greeting.json`. The 20 `common` ones are the default selection. Each has a direct `https://vk.com/sticker/1-<id>-512` preview.\n    - Telegram: greeting sticker **set names**, each with its `t.me/addstickers` link.\n    - Greeting texts in en/ru/zh/hi/vi.\n  - **`detect.js`** recognises incoming greetings (vk-bot's Russian regex, plus en/zh/hi/vi, a bare 👋 and known greeting stickers).\n  - **`plan.js`** holds the planner. It is pure, so a preview shows exactly what a send would do.\n    - `initiate` mode greets chats never written to first, oldest first; vk-bot calls this \"greet friends\".\n    - `reply` mode answers unanswered greetings in the language they were written in; this is vk-bot's greeting trigger.\n    - What a network does not allow becomes a skip reason instead of a failed send: WhatsApp/Messenger 24 h window, Zalo 48 h window, no sticker and no text.\n  - **`index.js`**: `runGreetings` sends with a 30 s pause by default, as vk-bot does. It records `greeting:<network>:<chat>` so nobody is greeted twice. `listLiveGreetingStickers` lists stickers live.\n- **Adapters**: VK, Telegram, WhatsApp and Messenger can now send stickers and parse incoming ones.\n  - VK lists greeting stickers live with `store.getStickersKeywords`. Telegram uses `getStickerSet`, keeping stickers whose emoji is 👋 🖐 🖖 🙋 🤚 ✋ 🙌.\n  - Telegram `file_id`s are specific to each bot, so they are always listed through the API, never collected in advance.\n- **Server**: six `/api/greetings/*` routes (catalogue, selection GET/PUT, live stickers, plan/send).\n  - `GET /api/greetings/file?id=` proxies Telegram thumbnails, so the bot token never reaches the browser.\n  - The CSP `img-src` adds only `https://vk.com`.\n- **CLI**: `greetings-stickers`, `greetings-select`, `greetings-plan`, `greetings-send`.\n- **SPA**: a **Greetings** screen (en/ru/zh/hi) where the user:\n  - sees and picks stickers (built-in, listed live, and previously picked);\n  - picks the Telegram sets, the language, and whether to send a sticker or text;\n  - previews who would be greeted, then sends.\n- **No artwork in the repository.** Every picture is a vk.com link or comes through the thumbnail proxy. The test fixtures generate their PNGs in code.\n\n### Telegram's empty-chat stickers (known gap)\n\nThe stickers Telegram suggests on an empty chat come from `messages.getStickers` with the emoticon `👋⭐️` (TDLib: `getGreetingStickers`). That is an MTProto **user** API call, and the Bot API cannot reach it. A bot also cannot start a conversation, so Telegram is reply-only in the planner. The screen says so and offers live listing of greeting sets instead. Supporting it would need a user-account client (TDLib), a separate integration with its own login flow.\n\n### X, WhatsApp, Zalo\n\n- **X**: DMs (`POST /2/dm_conversations/with/{id}/messages`) carry no sticker type, so X greets with text.\n- **WhatsApp**: stickers by media id or `.webp` link, within the 24 h customer-service window.\n- **Zalo**: researched and catalogued (`attachment_id`, 48 h window). The project has no Zalo adapter yet, so nothing can be sent there.\n\n### A regression this PR found and fixed\n\nThe first real-browser run showed the SPA stuck on its static fallback.\n\n- **Cause:** `dom.js` imported `greetings/index.js`, which pulls in every adapter. `github.js` and `upwork.js` call `new Function()` when they load, and the CSP (no `unsafe-eval`) rejects that, so the app never started.\n- **Fix:** the browser-safe half now lives in `greetings/plan.js`.\n- **Test:** a new test imports every screen under `node --disallow-code-generation-from-strings`. It fails with the old import and passes now.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm test`: 567/567 pass after merging `main`. New tests:\n  - `greetings.test.js`: catalogue, detection, planning, sending, adapters;\n  - `greetings-server.test.js`: routes, thumbnail proxy, CSP;\n  - `greetings-cli.test.js`;\n  - `greetings-web.test.js`: every locale, plus the CSP test.\n- `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check` and `npm run check:duplication` all pass.\n- `RUN_BROWSER_E2E=1 npm run test:e2e:greetings` runs a real server and headless Chromium with fake adapters. It:\n  1. loads real vk.com previews;\n  2. lists stickers live with proxied Telegram thumbnails;\n  3. saves a selection;\n  4. previews the plan with the WhatsApp chat skipped;\n  5. sends, and asserts the exact posts (`vk:200, vk:100, telegram:77` with the picked sticker) and the recorded greeting link.\n- `node examples/greetings-preview.mjs` prints both plans for a seeded store.\n- Logs: [`docs/case-studies/issue-35/verification-logs/`](https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/tree/issue-35-9b770690b2d5/docs/case-studies/issue-35/verification-logs).\n\n## Screenshot\n\nThe Greetings screen in headless Chromium after a live listing and a send. VK stickers come straight from vk.com; the two Telegram discs are fixture thumbnails served through the proxy.\n\n![Greetings screen](https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/blob/issue-35-9b770690b2d5/docs/screenshots/issue-35/greetings.png?raw=true)\n\n## Documentation\n\n- [`docs/GREETINGS.md`](https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/blob/issue-35-9b770690b2d5/docs/GREETINGS.md) (+ ru/zh/hi)\n- USER-GUIDE section 10 \"Greet people with a hi or a sticker\", in all four languages\n- README bullets, changeset (minor)\n\n## Known gap\n\n- Telegram's own empty-chat suggestions need the MTProto user API (see above).\n- There is no Zalo adapter.\n- The Rust server does not have the `/api/greetings/*` routes yet. Without them, the SPA falls back to the local store for the catalogue, the selection and the preview, and says that listing and sending need the JS server.\n",
