      "updated_at": "2026-10-11T17:36:09Z",
      "body": "<!-- hive-mind:working-session-summary -->\n## Working session summary\n\nPR #36 now supports greeting people with a \"hi\" or a greeting sticker across the supported networks, and it's marked ready for review: https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/pull/36. All three CI workflows pass on the latest commit (e9e343e), main is merged in, and there are no comments on the issue or the PR.\n\n**What it adds:**\n- **Planning:** it greets chats that were never written to (oldest first), or answers unanswered greetings in the language they came in. Network limits, like WhatsApp's and Messenger's 24-hour window or Telegram bots only being able to reply, show up as skipped chats in the preview instead of failed sends.\n- **Sending:** a 30-second pause between messages by default, as in konard/vk-bot. Each sent greeting is recorded so nobody is greeted twice.\n- **Stickers:** the VK greeting stickers come from vk-bot's catalogue. VK and Telegram greeting stickers can also be listed live through their APIs. No image files are in the repo:\n```text\n  - VK pictures are direct `vk.com/sticker/...` links;\n  - Telegram thumbnails go through the user's own server, so the bot token never reaches the browser.\n- **Where to use it:** a new Greetings screen in the web app (pick stickers, preview, send), four CLI commands, and six server routes.\n- **Docs:** a new guide in all four languages, a new user-guide section, README bullets, an example script, and a case study with the research and verification logs.\n```\n\n**A bug I introduced and fixed:** the first real-browser run showed that my earlier pushed commit broke the whole web app. The page's Content Security Policy forbids `new Function`. The greetings code made the app load every network adapter, and two of them (GitHub, Upwork) call it when loaded. My unit tests render the screen without a browser, so they didn't catch it. I moved the browser-safe part into `js/src/greetings/plan.js` and added a test that loads every screen with string evaluation disabled. It failed before the fix and passes now; it runs only on Node, because Deno and Bun don't take that flag.\n\n**Tested:** 567 of 567 tests pass after merging main, along with lint, formatting and the duplication check. The headless Chromium run passed: it loads real vk.com previews, lists stickers live, saves a selection, previews the plan and sends. The screenshot from that run is in the PR description.\n\n**Not done:**\n- **Telegram's empty-chat stickers:** the issue asked for these, but Telegram only offers them through its user-account API, which a bot can't call. The screen says so and offers greeting sticker sets to choose from instead. Adding them would need a separate user-account integration with its own login.\n- **Zalo:** researched and listed in the network table, but there's no Zalo adapter, so nothing is sent there.\n- **X:** it has no stickers in direct messages, so it gets text greetings only.\n- **Rust server:** it doesn't have the greetings routes yet. Without them, the web app can still preview a plan from local data but can't list stickers live or send.\n\nOne side effect on this machine: getting a browser for the test briefly removed the globally installed Playwright browsers. I've reinstalled them (Chromium, Firefox, WebKit, ffmpeg).\n\n---\n*This summary was automatically extracted from the AI working session output.*",
